            <ArticleTitle>Diabetes and cancer: a 2013 synopsis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>247-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.dsx.2013.08.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1871-4021(13)00087-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diabetes, in particular type 2 diabetes, and cancer are two diseases that appear to be associated. Numerous epidemiological studies indicate indeed that diabetes increases the incidence of several tumors. Chronic hyperglycemia and/or insulin resistance with compensatory hyperinsulinemia could account for the association. On the other hand, the interpretation of the link between diabetes and cancer could be influenced by therapeutical interferences. Considering all these data together, cancer should be considered as a &quot;new potential complication&quot; of diabetes and integrated in the follow-up of diabetic subjects.</AbstractText>
